@kraftverk/integration-apple-media

Ported to TypeScript from:

- pyatv (https://github.com/postlund/pyatv), Copyright Pierre Ståhl,
  licensed under the MIT License: Companion's frames and messages, OPACK,
  HomeKit's pairing as the Apple TV takes it, and the remote's session.
- Home Assistant's `apple_tv` integration
  (https://github.com/home-assistant/core/tree/dev/homeassistant/components/apple_tv),
  Copyright the Home Assistant authors, licensed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0: how it is found and paired.

Test vectors: test/hap-vectors.ts holds HomeKit's SRP vectors as fast-srp
(https://github.com/homebridge/fast-srp, MIT License) publishes them.

Uses, unchanged, as dependencies: @noble/hashes, @noble/curves and
@noble/ciphers (https://paulmillr.com/noble/), Copyright Paul Miller,
MIT License.

Changed: rewritten in TypeScript for kraftverk's device model — pure, over
a byte channel, pairing as a setup action in turns. No code was copied
verbatim; the protocol's behaviour follows pyatv's.

